   [
    0.1,
    "Chapter one, lesson two."
   ],
   [
    2.12,
    "Structural classification: the side chains."
   ],
   [
    5.284,
    "Picture a box of building bricks."
   ],
   [
    7.472,
    "Every brick has the same base, the same studs underneath, so they all snap together."
   ],
   [
    12.654,
    "But on top, each brick carries a different shape."
   ],
   [
    15.779,
    "An amino acid is just like that."
   ],
   [
    18.032,
    "Every one has the same backbone: the amino group, the carboxyl group, the alpha carbon and a hydrogen."
   ],
   [
    24.633,
    "What makes it different is the side chain, called R."
   ],
   [
    27.706,
    "Here is our amino acid card from lesson one."
   ],
   [
    30.376,
    "Today we light the first tab, Structural: sorting amino acids by the shape of R."
   ],
   [
    35.675,
    "The slide sorts them into four families: aliphatic, aromatic, heterocyclic and imino."
   ]
  ]
